1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,280
India has two massive coastlines.

2
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:04,390
So why does one face cyclones more often?

3
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:06,810
The eastern coastline
faces the Bay of Bengal,

4
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:09,770
while the western coastline
faces the Arabian Sea.

5
00:00:09,970 --> 00:00:11,940
Both can produce dangerous cyclones.

6
00:00:12,010 --> 00:00:12,840
But historically,

7
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:17,580
the Bay of Bengal has been more favourable
for cyclone formation and intensification.

8
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:21,530
Its warm waters and atmospheric
conditions help fuel powerful storms.

9
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:23,920
That's why states like Odisha,
West Bengal,

10
00:00:24,170 --> 00:00:27,920
Andhra Pradesh and Tamil Nadu have
faced numerous destructive cyclones.

11
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:32,260
The west coast isn't safe either,
but the historical pattern is different.

12
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,170
Which coastal state do you think
is most vulnerable to cyclones?

